==English==

===Etymology===
c. 1200, from {{inh|en|enm|therwith}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þǣrwiþ||therewith, in return, in exchange, against
}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|there|with}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|derved||therewith}}, {{cog|sv|därvid||therewith, thereby}}. Parallel with Dutch {{m|nl|daarmee}}, German {{m|de|damit||therewith}}, though etymologically different. See also {{l|en|theremid}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ðɛəˈwɪθ/|/ðɛəˈwɪð/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-therewith.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-therewith.wav|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪð|ɪθ|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[with|With]] this, that or those.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Philippians|4|11|passage=I have learned, in whatever state I am, '''therewith''' to be content.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1876|title=A concise law dictionary by Herbert Newman Mozley and George Crispe Whiteley, barrister at law
|passage=In untechnical language, we may describe [[letters of horning]] as the authority by which a person, directed by the decree of a court of justice to pay or perform anything, is ordered to comply '''therewith'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=The Vigilantes at the Capitol Grounds|title=The “City Guard”: A History of Company “B”, First Regiment Infantry, N.G.C. [National Guard of California]: During the Sacramento Campaign, July 3 to 26, 1894{{nb...|Including a Brief History of the Company since Its Organization, March 31, 1854, to July 3, 1894}}|location=San Francisco, Calif.|publisher=Filmer-Rollins Electrotype Co.{{nb...|typographers, electrotypers and stereotypers, 474 Sansome St., San Francisco}}|year=1895|pages=79–80|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=eqQ1AQAAIAAJ&pg=PA80|oclc=8189412|passage=At the expiration of the solemn ceremonies connected '''therewith''' Private Flanagan of the Irish tent arose, and, after congratulating the learned doctors of the Keeley Club on the success of the meeting, invited all present to attend a pink tea that would be held in his tent that evening at eight {{smallcaps|p.m.}}}}
# In [[addition]] to that; besides, moreover.
# [[thereupon|Thereupon]], [[forthwith]]; with that being said or done.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1869|passage='I take the privilege, Mistress Ruth, of saluting you.' ...And '''therewith''' I bussed her well.|author=w:Richard Blackmore|title=Lorna Doone|page=1}}

